exit: 0
--- stdout
commandments hints — Auto-fix the Spatie Data magic surface — rename non-`from…` object factories to `from<Type>`, rewrite their call sites to `::from(...)`, and regenerate the `@method from(...)`/`collect(...)` docblock hints.

Usage:
  commandments hints [path]         apply the fixes (the default — this WRITES)
  commandments hints [path] --dry-run[=FILE]
                                    preview a unified diff instead, to the screen or a file

Options:
  --changes                   only files changed in the working tree (alias: --git)
  --branch[=BASE]             only files new/changed on this branch vs BASE (default: main)
  --branch=REPO:[BASE..]HEAD  only files HEAD changed since it left BASE (default: main) in the
                              repository REPO, a folder under the path with its own .git
  --pr=REPO#N                 only the files pull request N changes in the repository REPO, asked of
                              GitHub with gh
  --repent[=ID]               only the files listed in a past run's checklist (bare: the latest)
  --dry-run[=FILE]            preview the rewrite as a unified diff instead of applying it

  A scoped run (--changes/--branch) is forced to docblock-only: a rename's call sites can live
  outside the scope, so renaming is whole-tree only. `repent` runs this as one of its scribes;
  `hints` is the focused Data-only entry.

